# Next App Router Patterns

- Prefer Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only for browser APIs, local interactive state, effects, or client-only providers.
- Keep `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, and modal route files thin. Move reusable UI into `src/components/` or `src/features/`.
- Read route params/search params at the route boundary, then pass typed props downward instead of re-reading them deep in the tree.
- Use `@/` imports for app code and keep imports grouped: React/Next, third-party, internal.
- Reuse shared guards/providers already present in the app shell instead of duplicating auth or layout wiring in feature pages.

```tsx
// Good: thin route component
export default function Page() {
  return <PipelineListPage />;
}
```

```tsx
// Add "use client" only when needed
"use client";
import { useState } from "react";
```
